* Redirected damage is calculated by taking the pre-mitigation damage against the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}, applying ''Test of Spirit's'' damage modifier, and then capping it to the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} {{as|'''current''' health}}. This damage will then be affected by damage modifiers (resistances and other effects) of the {{as|Vessel|buzzword3}}.
** This order of operations allows ''Test of Spirit'' to deal more or less percentage of the {{as|Vessel's|buzzword3}} {{as|health}} than would be expected:
**# Because the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} modifiers can be different from the {{as|Vessel's|buzzword3}}, allowing the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} to have higher or lower [[health|effective health]], respectively increasing or decreasing the maximum pre-mitigated damage from killing it.
**# Because, while it would be expected to block excess pre-mitigated damage over what kills the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}}, since the cap does not consider the {{as|Spirit's|buzzword}} damage modifier, it may cause it to block damage before the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} is killed [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=y2ASLYcuTXE], or in corner cases not block excess damage even if it is killed. On the other hand, ''Test of Spirit's'' damage modifier is unexpectedly applied before the cap instead of after, with the same effect of potentially causing the cap to not block excess damage even if the {{as|Spirit|buzzword}} is killed, or in corner cases block damage before it is killed.
**#* The addition of the two, causes an increasing difference of expected damage when the pre-mitigated damage is between <code>Spirit current health{{divided by}}Spiritmod</code> and <code>Spirit current health{{divided by}}Emod</code>. {{bug|2}}|affectedEffects=Illaoi E|estimatedPatchOrigin=V5.23|<!--added automatically-->wikiUploadTimestamp=1773991211|<!--added automatically-->pagename=Template:Data Illaoi/Test of Spirit
}}
